---
import BrainfuckCompiler from '../components/BrainfuckCompiler.svelte';
import mandelbrot from '../data/mandelbrot.bf?raw';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Optimizing Brainfuck Compiler"
	description="An optimizing Brainfuck-to-WebAssembly compiler running in the browser."
>
	<article class="tool-container pt-8 pb-10 sm:pt-10 sm:pb-12">
		<h1 class="page-heading mx-auto text-center text-3xl sm:text-4xl">
			Optimizing Brainfuck Compiler
		</h1>
		<div
			class="post-prose mt-4 space-y-2 text-base leading-7 text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400"
		>
			<p>
				This optimizing Brainfuck compiler runs entirely in the browser and
				targets WebAssembly as its output format. The generated WebAssembly is
				executed by the same browser runtime that hosts the compiler itself. I
				wrote it for
				<a class="text-link" href="https://users.cs.utah.edu/~regehr/"
					>John Regehr’s</a
				>
				advanced compilers course (<a
					class="text-link"
					href="https://github.com/dominicmkennedy/bf-interpreter/"
					>source code</a
				>).
			</p>
			<p>The optimizer uses an IR to recognize Brainfuck idioms, including:</p>
			<ul
				class="list-disc space-y-0.5 pl-5 marker:text-[var(--heading-secondary-start)]"
			>
				<li>
					clearing a cell with a decrement loop
					<code>[-]</code>
				</li>
				<li>
					using a loop to multiply and transfer values
					<code>[- > + &lt;]</code>
				</li>
				<li>
					using SIMD to scan for zero cells more quickly
					<code>[>]</code>
				</li>
			</ul>
		</div>
		<BrainfuckCompiler initialProgram={mandelbrot} client:load />
	</article>
</BaseLayout>
